From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:36:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: keep a single implicit BF row at 160 MHz

For implicit beamforming of a VHT station at 160 MHz,
mt7915_mcu_sta_bfer_vht() sets ibf_nrow to 1, but
mt7915_mcu_sta_bfer_tlv() then overwrote it with the number of tx
antennas, so the special case never reached the firmware.

Set the default before the per-mode setup instead of after it. Only
matters with implicit beamforming on (debugfs, off by default). Un-skip
mt7915_test_bfer_vht_160_ibf.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mcu.c            | 3 ++-
 mt7915/tests/mcu-test.c | 6 ++----
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/mcu.c b/mt7915/mcu.c
index 3ac49e6a..eb3154c1 100644
--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -1310,6 +1310,8 @@ mt7915_mcu_sta_bfer_tlv(struct mt7915_dev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb,
 
 	tlv = mt76_connac_mcu_add_tlv(skb, STA_REC_BF, sizeof(*bf));
 	bf = (struct sta_rec_bf *)tlv;
+	/* all tx antennas, unless the mode's setup below picks fewer */
+	bf->ibf_nrow = tx_ant;
 
 	if (sta->deflink.he_cap.has_he && ebf)
 		mt7915_mcu_sta_bfer_he(sta, vc, bf);
@@ -1321,7 +1323,6 @@ mt7915_mcu_sta_bfer_tlv(struct mt7915_dev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb,
 	bf->bf_cap = ebf ? ebf : dev->ibf << 1;
 	bf->bw = sta->deflink.bandwidth;
 	bf->ibf_dbw = sta->deflink.bandwidth;
-	bf->ibf_nrow = tx_ant;
 
 	if (!ebf && sta->deflink.bandwidth <= IEEE80211_STA_RX_BW_40 && !bf->ncol)
 		bf->ibf_timeout = 0x48;
diff --git a/mt7915/tests/mcu-test.c b/mt7915/tests/mcu-test.c
index 3ed4e431..fb44eb82 100644
--- a/mt7915/tests/mcu-test.c
+++ b/mt7915/tests/mcu-test.c
@@ -3436,16 +3436,14 @@ static void mt7915_test_bfer_vht(struct kunit *test)
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_NULL(test, mt7915_test_bf_tlv(test, &c));
 }
 
-/* Implicit 160 MHz VHT beamforming is meant to use a single implicit row
- * (bfer_vht sets ibf_nrow = 1), but bfer_tlv overwrites it with tx_ant.
+/* Implicit 160 MHz VHT beamforming uses a single implicit row (bfer_vht
+ * sets ibf_nrow = 1), not one per tx antenna.
  */
 static void mt7915_test_bfer_vht_160_ibf(struct kunit *test)
 {
 	struct mt7915_test_ctx c;
 	struct sta_rec_bf *bf;
 
-	kunit_skip(test, "driver bug: 160 MHz iBF ibf_nrow = 1 is overwritten by tx_ant");
-
 	mt7915_test_init(test, &c, NL80211_BAND_5GHZ, NL80211_IFTYPE_AP);
 	mt7915_test_ht(c.sta);
 	mt7915_test_vht(c.sta);
